---
description: Keep ASCII/box-drawing diagrams column-aligned; never leave uneven padding before borders.
alwaysApply: true
---

# ASCII diagram alignment

When drawing ASCII or box-drawing diagrams (tables, UI mockups, trees, borders with `┌┐└┘│─├┤┬┴┼`, etc.), every vertical border must line up with the corresponding corners on the rows above and below. Pad cell contents with spaces so the right edge closes flush - never leave a column short ("outspaced").

**Wrong** - right border drifts left of the top/bottom edge:

```
┌──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ABC-2856       ▾ │ Search repositories...                    │
└──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Right** - content padded so `│` aligns with `┐` / `┘`:

```
┌──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ABC-2856       ▾ │ Search repositories...                     │
└──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Checklist before shipping a diagram**

- Count characters per row (including borders); every row in a closed box must be the same width.
- Multi-column boxes: each column's width is fixed by the longest header/separator for that column; shorter cells get trailing spaces.
- Prefer a monospace-safe character count over visual eyeballing in a proportional font.
- Fix alignment when editing an existing diagram; do not leave one crooked line.
